1
00:01:56,602 --> 00:01:59,254
<v Man>Green Travel Agency. What can I do for you?

2
00:01:59,254 --> 00:02:07,803
<v Woman>Hi, good morning. My family and I intend to go on a vacation for Vancouver, and could you please help us reserve a hotel?

3
00:02:07,803 --> 00:02:14,726
<v Man>Sure, with pleasure. First, I’ll take some notes down of your personal details. May I have your full name, please?

4
00:02:14,726 --> 00:02:15,873
<v Woman>Anna Hardie.

5
00:02:15,873 --> 00:02:23,448
<v Man>Hi Anna, there is a hotel in Vancouver named Holiday Chilcotin, which is very popular with guests on vacation


6
00:02:23,448 --> 00:02:26,385
<v Woman>Mmm, Chilcotin, can you spell it?


7
00:02:26,385 --> 00:02:32,845
<v Man>C-H-I-L-C-O-T-I-N, a local hotel


8
00:02:32,845 --> 00:02:42,261
<v Woman>Where is it? Is it in the downtown? You see, my family member prefers to stay in a quieter zone during vacation. Not too buzzy you know.


9
00:02:42,261 --> 00:02:47,913
<v Man>Uh, no worries. Actually it’s ten miles from the city centre, near a train station.


10
00:02:47,913 --> 00:02:54,316
<v Woman>Oh, I think that’s okay. I am travelling with my husband. Is it expensive to live in that hotel?


11
00:02:54,306 --> 00:03:06,416
<v Man>Well, in your case, I think a double room would suit you well. Normally, it’s 210 dollars, but if you can make a reservation in advance, you can pay 169 dollars for a night.


12
00:03:06,406 --> 00:03:16,119
<v Woman>That sounds pretty reasonable. I’d like to book for 5 days from 27 June through 1 July. Are there still rooms available?


13
00:03:16,119 --> 00:03:21,866
<v Man>Oh, let me check. Ah, yes, they still have some vacant rooms. Would you like to book it now?


14
00:03:21,866 --> 00:03:26,158
<v Woman>Wait. One more question: any meals are included in the price?


15
00:03:26,158 --> 00:03:33,506
<v Man>Well, you need to pay separately for lunch and dinner, except the breakfast, which is provided from 7 to 9.


16
00:03:33,506 --> 00:03:39,247
<v Woman>Alright, please book it for me. Is there anything we can do near the hotel?


17
00:03:39,247 --> 00:03:45,042
<v Man>Yeah, it only takes 10 minutes to walk to a science museum sponsored by the city council.


18
00:03:45,042 --> 00:03:48,343
<v Woman>Excellent, I think my husband will love it.


19
00:04:30,648 --> 00:04:37,078
<v Woman>Are there any outdoor activities to recommend to us? Because we don’t like to stay in the hotel for all day.


20
00:04:37,078 --> 00:04:48,271
<v Man>Oh, yes. If you like to go cycling there is a shop near the hotel, where you can rent a bike. Helmets are on sales, but you‘ll have to take your own boots.


21
00:04:48,271 --> 00:04:51,493
<v Woman>That sounds great. I think I’ll do that


22
00:04:51,493 --> 00:04:56,521
<v Man>Also, It’s a charming plae for visitors who like to go mountain climbing


23
00:04:56,521 --> 00:04:58,215
<v Woman>Oh, awesome!


24
00:04:58,215 --> 00:05:10,121
<v Man>The hotel prepares two trips to a nearby mountain. One trip starts at 9 in the morning, and the other one is at 2 in the afternoon each day. You can just call reception to make a reservation. 

25
00:05:10,121 --> 00:05:21,913
<v Man>And it’s free of charge, but please be careful of fires, which are not allowed. If you like, you can go fishing in the lakes. For camping, a tent can be borrowed for a rest from the driver.


26
00:05:21,913 --> 00:05:25,311
<v Woman>Oh, I can’t wait. It sounds like a lot of fun!


27
00:05:25,311 --> 00:05:33,527
<v Man>If you’d like some adventure, you can go hiking in the forest. Sometimes you can even see some black bears. Be careful.


28
00:05:33,517 --> 00:05:38,168
<v Woman>Oh my god, we really do not like to take risks while travelling.


29
00:05:38,168 --> 00:05:45,892
<v Man>One last thing. There is a visit to an ancient gold mine every afternoon. If you are interested, just call reception.


30
00:05:45,892 --> 00:05:49,412
<v Woman>I think we will do that. Thank you so much for your help.


31
00:05:49,412 --> 00:05:51,592
<v Man>You are more than welcome...